  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/res7300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Res 7301.14 Fires",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-01-23",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Res 7301.14 Fires.\n\n(a) Fires shall be permitted only in places provided or designated for that purpose, unless posted as prohibited during times determined by the division of forests and lands for resource protection, such as but not limited to, forest fire danger.\n\n(b) Portable grills shall be permitted, provided that the DRED property or beach area has places provided or designated for use of grills and that the ash and unused charcoal are emptied only into unused fireplaces or receptacles provided for that purpose.\n\n(c) The burning of rubbish, garbage, trash, debris, or any other discarded, refuse or waste material of every kind and description shall not be permitted.\n\nSource. #6167 eff 1-18-96, EXPIRED: 1-18-04\n\nNew. #8127, INTERIM, eff 7-27-04, EXPIRED: 1-23-05\n\nNew. #8532, eff 1-1-06 (from Res 7301.11); ss by #10532, eff 3-1-14",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/res7300.html"
